# Export rules for snapshot syncs.
#
# .gitignore has NO effect on files that are already tracked, and plan.md is
# tracked deliberately (it should live on Gitea). These export-ignore rules are
# what actually keep it out of the curated public snapshot, so anything built
# with `git archive` or a filtered `git ls-files` cannot leak it by accident.
#
# .github/ is deliberately NOT excluded: the public repo is meant to run its
# own GitHub Actions, so its workflows must survive the snapshot. Only Gitea's
# CI config is stripped, because it is useless off this instance.
plan.md          export-ignore
*.internal.md    export-ignore
.gitea/          export-ignore
.gitignore       export-ignore
.dockerignore    export-ignore
